{# The UPGRADE overlay - the album overlay plus one line.

   `upgrade_releases` re-imports every bare track through the album overlay, and
   that path is used by `media-sync --upgrade`, `--retag` (the weekly cron) and
   the maintenance flow. config.yaml sets lastgenre.force: yes, so without this
   override each of those runs re-derives genres from Last.fm and REPLACES them -
   in library.db and, because write: yes, in the files - for every track it
   re-imports. A re-match must not rewrite metadata it was not asked to change.

   It is its own overlay rather than a line in album.yaml on purpose: album.yaml
   is also the nightly release pass's overlay, where new downloads SHOULD get
   Last.fm genres. Keeping them apart is what stops one run's needs from
   silently changing the other's behaviour.
#}
{% include "album.yaml.j2" %}
lastgenre:
    auto: no
